 "_note": "exp60 oracle field boxes (critic EXP60-PREP-01): one box per needed field of the 24 transcribed pictures, by a fixed CPU rule on the original pixels -- never from reading results. Text = dark, unsaturated pixels (max channel < 110, channel spread < 40); the picture is split at its middle column (sample A / Pair 1 left, sample B / Pair 2 right); in each half the rows holding text form bands (gaps of >= 3 text-free rows separate them).   temperature: the half's last two bands below its middle are the mass line and the speed line (EXP45 / 51 semantics:                the whole field text line of that sample);   magnets:     the half's last band is the distance label band (the \"|- 42.8 mm -|\" label of that pair). Box = the band's text extent in that half, padded by 2 px and clipped: [x0, y0, w, h] in original pixels (reading's pixel_box / region convention). Source: computed by this rule, previews looked at by Claude Code; not checked by a person.",
